builder/build/.sccache
build/

# In-source CMake build artifacts. builder/build.sh configures in-source
# (`cd /src && cmake .`), so a local dev build leaves these in the working
# tree. The packaging build (builder/dockerfile.*.build) does `COPY . /src`,
# which would otherwise drag a stale CMakeCache.txt into the image and poison
# a fresh configure — e.g. a cache with HAVE_PAM=ON makes CMake compile pam.c
# in the packaging image, which intentionally has no libpam0g-dev, breaking the
# build. Excluding them forces a clean configure in every Docker build context.
# NOTE: do NOT add `*.cmake` here — cmake/*.cmake are tracked source files.
CMakeCache.txt
**/CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
**/CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
**/cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
**/CTestTestfile.cmake
xorg.build/
